;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Subsidiary Lion Homes undergoing liquidation with unaudited 2023/24 and missing 2024/25 financial statements, consolidated on break-up basis","lead":"A subsidiary in liquidation with unaudited financial statements creates material uncertainty in group borrowing capacity and financial position; group accounts can only receive partial assurance because auditors cannot verify subsidiary valuations.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"Appendix A - 2025-26 Audit Progress Report","paper_url":"https://cmis.norwich.gov.uk/Live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=ytSfyOJbyM5W%2fZGs6sEYJW4NBkHtR3OvGd6p4Q9lv84ir3uKTaIYYw%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"15 September 2026","paper_title":"Appendix A - 2025-26 Audit Progress Report","paper_url":"https://cmis.norwich.gov.uk/Live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=ytSfyOJbyM5W%2fZGs6sEYJW4NBkHtR3OvGd6p4Q9lv84ir3uKTaIYYw%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Property, Plant and Equipment (\u00a31,075 million) and Investment Property (\u00a396 million) can only receive partial assurance; material assets remain unaudited due to valuation cycle disruption from 2021/22 disclaimer","detail":"Major balance sheet assets totalling \u00a31.17 billion cannot receive substantial audit assurance. The auditors note that due to the valuation cycle, many assets have not been subject to revaluation or audit procedures since the 2021/22 disclaimer. The auditors state the maximum assurance achievable is partial.","category":"audit","matters":"These are the council's largest asset classes; partial audit assurance on \u00a31.17bn of assets indicates unresolved valuation issues and limits lender confidence in the balance sheet.","figures":"PPE net book value \u00a31,075.25 million; Investment Property \u00a396.20 million","quote":"The maximum assurance level we will be able to report in 2025/26 will be partial, as due to the valuations cycle in place at the Council, there are a number of assets that have not been subject to revaluation in the period that, following previous disclaimers of opinion, have not been subject to audit procedures.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"15 September 2026","paper_title":"Appendix A - 2025-26 Audit Progress Report","paper_url":"https://cmis.norwich.gov.uk/Live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=ytSfyOJbyM5W%2fZGs6sEYJW4NBkHtR3OvGd6p4Q9lv84ir3uKTaIYYw%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Auditors unable to obtain substantial assurance over council reserves, with only partial assurance expected, persisting from 2021/22 disclaimer of opinion","detail":"The auditors explicitly state they cannot provide substantial assurance over the council's useable and unusable reserves pending completion of work to rebuild assurance following a disclaimer issued in 2021/22\u2014three years ago. Reserves are expected to receive only Partial assurance in 2025/26.","category":"audit","matters":"Reserves are the council's financial shock absorber and directly affect its resilience and borrowing capacity; inability to audit them properly after three years represents a material audit limitation and suggests unresolved governance issues.","figures":"Expected assurance rating 2025/26: Partial (vs Substantial for most other account areas)","quote":"Until we have completed our work programme on the rebuilding of assurance following the disclaimed audit opinions, we are unable to obtain substantial assurance over the useable and unusable reserves of the Council reported in the financial statements.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"15 September 2026","paper_title":"Appendix A - 2025-26 Audit Progress Report","paper_url":"https://cmis.norwich.gov.uk/Live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=ytSfyOJbyM5W%2fZGs6sEYJW4NBkHtR3OvGd6p4Q9lv84ir3uKTaIYYw%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Subsidiary Lion Homes undergoing liquidation with unaudited 2023/24 and missing 2024/25 financial statements, consolidated on break-up basis","detail":"Lion Homes (Norwich) Ltd is in Members' Voluntary Liquidation. Its 2023/24 financial statements have not been audited and filed. No 2024/25 financial statements have been prepared. The company has been consolidated into group accounts on a break-up basis rather than a going-concern basis, which auditors could not fully assure.","category":"governance","matters":"A subsidiary in liquidation with unaudited financial statements creates material uncertainty in group borrowing capacity and financial position; group accounts can only receive partial assurance because auditors cannot verify subsidiary valuations.","figures":"Auditors can only provide Partial expected assurance rating for Group financial statements and consolidation","quote":"Lion Homes (Norwich) Ltd is currently undergoing a Members' Voluntary Liquidation process. The Company's financial statements for 2023/24 have not been audited and filed. The 2024/25 financial statements have not yet been prepared. As a result, no subsidiary auditor reporting was prepared for 2024/25. The company has therefore been consolidated into the Group financial statements on a break-up basis.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"15 September 2026","paper_title":"Supplementary Agenda Document Pack - Audit committee - 15/09/2026","paper_url":"https://cmis.norwich.gov.uk/Live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=9gIsSsyMkYHLLpO8rJay7VfhgxHPJo%2fMGEngkhWR7C9j40daLc6RoA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Group financial statements consolidation work incomplete; expected only Partial assurance in 2025/26","detail":"EY issued no assurance on group financial statements in 2024/25 and expects only Partial assurance in 2025/26. Work remains dependent on receiving component auditors' reporting deliverables within agreed timescales. The auditors' ability to conclude depends on subsidiary and related-entity audit work being completed.","category":"governance","matters":"If the group accounts cannot be fully assured, stakeholders cannot rely on a complete, audited view of all council and subsidiary activities and financial position. This is particularly acute given the ongoing liquidation of a subsidiary.","figures":"Group financial statements: None (2023/24), None (2024/25), Partial expected (2025/26)","quote":"We are currently completing our testing in this area and expect to obtain assurance over the closing balance as at 31 March 2026, subject to the satisfactory completion of our remaining audit procedures and review processes. This is dependent on receiving the component auditor's reporting deliverables in accordance with the agreed timetable.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"15 September 2026","paper_title":"Supplementary Agenda Document Pack - Audit committee - 15/09/2026","paper_url":"https://cmis.norwich.gov.uk/Live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zNRBcoShgo=9gIsSsyMkYHLLpO8rJay7VfhgxHPJo%2fMGEngkhWR7C9j40daLc6RoA%3d%3d&amp;rUzwRPf%2bZ3zd4E7Ikn8Lyw%3d%3d=pwRE6AGJFLDNlh225F5QMaQWCtPHwdhUfCZ%2fLUQzgA2uL5jNRG4jdQ%3d%3d&amp;mCTIbCubSFfXsDGW9IXnlg%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;kCx1AnS9%2fpWZQ40DXFvdEw%3d%3d=hFflUdN3100%3d&amp;uJovDxwdjMPoYv%2bAJvYtyA%3d%3d=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;FgPlIEJYlotS%2bYGoBi5olA%3d%3d=NHdURQburHA%3d&amp;d9Qjj0ag1Pd993jsyOJqFvmyB7X0CSQK=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNR9xqBux0r1Q8Za60lavYmz=ctNJFf55vVA%3d&amp;WGewmoAfeNQ16B2MHuCpMRKZMwaG1PaO=ctNJFf55vVA%3d","headline":"Reserves cannot be fully assured; auditors rebuilding assurance following disclaimed audit opinion","detail":"The Council's useable and unusable reserves cannot be given substantial assurance in 2025/26 because the auditors are still on a programme to rebuild assurance following the disclaimed opinion. Reserves remain at 'Partial' assurance level in the current year.","category":"reserves","matters":"Reserves are a key metric of financial resilience for local government finance. Inability to audit them reliably creates uncertainty about the true financial position available to meet future pressures or fund services.","figures":"Reserves: expected 'Partial' assurance in 2025/26; no assurance in 2023/24 or 2024/25; assurance rebuild following disclaimed opinion","quote":"Until we have completed our work programme on the rebuilding of assurance following the disclaimed audit opinions, we are unable to obtain substantial assurance over the useable and unusable reserves of the Council reported in the financial statements.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-15"},"name":"Norwich City","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-20","since_iso":"2026-08-21","distress":false,"headline":"Property, Plant and Equipment (\u00a31,075 million) and Investment Property (\u00a396 million) can only receive partial assurance; material assets remain unaudited due to valuation cycle disruption from 2021/22 disclaimer","lead":"These are the council's largest asset classes; partial audit assurance on \u00a31.17bn of assets indicates unresolved valuation issues and limits lender confidence in the balance sheet.","also":["40 other findings in this window"],"watch":null,"n_findings":41,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix A - 2025-26 Audit Progress Report","top_paper_url":"https://cmis.norwich.gov.uk/Live/Document.ashx?czJKcaeAi5tUFL1DTL2UE4zN